TELOMERE-CCC2-1:{"chunk":"c10","format":"ccc2-wire/1","records":[{"checksum":"cabffc7f07a3cb2517e575f2d3fe736fa60fc27900593a216d108bdbe788ae2f","id":"C1","kind":"claim","label":"The surviving form of the user's idea (12c): 3D foliated dynamical system, 2D leaves, flow generator (skew-adjoint) as the leaf-to-ambient link, closed orbits = primes, Ruelle zeta = zeta, explicit formula = Lefschetz trace -- this is Deninger's program","note":"formulate, do not simulate shadows (D8). Framework's computable content after 12d is exhausted; L4 remains as formulated conjecture.","status":"conjectural","type":"C"},{"checksum":"53baeace5f16f7283a835136ef74fd64b46c6085d5392cb5e274be8e8b38a18f","generates":[{"prescription":"take T^2 as the leaf, T^3 as the ambient, and the Node 11 checklist R1-R6 as the operator spec","stage":"fix objects"},{"prescription":"construct the five candidate leaf-to-ambient links: L1 product, L2 mapping torus (flat/Nil/Sol), L3 unit tangent bundle, L4 Deninger-type foliated dynamical system, L5 Heisenberg nilmanifold","stage":"enumerate linkages"}],"honest_boundary":"The original idea (link a 2-torus and a 3-torus by a self-adjoint operator) was never written down and is absent from the April 2026 archive -- rebuilt from a clean foundation. L4 is conjectural formulation only (D8: formulate, do not simulate shadows). The L1-L3 computable constructions are exact; the record as a whole is conjectural because L4 is load-bearing.","honest_label":"conjectural","id":"D1","rule":"objects T^2 (leaf; also the 10d Jacobian type), T^3 (ambient), operator spec = Node 11 checklist R1-R6","subtitle":"Multi-torus foundation (12a): the user's idea rebuilt from scratch","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"12a foundation","expected":"done 2026-09-30, documented in multi_torus_framework.md"}]},{"checksum":"394f89fbec2b2758cc78092f2933b7f639839b9715f8458c8060a2a6755cd134","generates":[{"prescription":"enumerate the lattice points of the flat-T^3 spectrum (554,981 points) and compare the first 300 eigenvalues against the first 300 zeta zeros (multi_torus_weyl.png)","stage":"count flat spectrum"},{"prescription":"compare dimensional counting rates against the zeros' (T/2pi) log T: d=2 grows too slowly by a log, d>=3 grows too fast","stage":"apply Weyl's law"}],"honest_boundary":"L1-L3 dead by theorem, not difficulty. EXACT loophole recorded in the framework doc and not closed here: zeros-as-subset of a higher-dimensional spectrum is not ruled out by Weyl's-law counting. Do not present the kill as closing subset embeddings.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D2","rule":"flat-T^3 Laplacian spectrum 2pi*sqrt(m^2+n^2+k^2); Weyl's law N(Lambda) ~ C_d Vol Lambda^{d/2} vs zeros' (T/2pi) log T","subtitle":"Weyl probe: no fixed-dimension manifold Laplacian has the zeros as its spectrum (12b)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"first 300 flat-T^3 eigenvalues vs first 300 zeta zeros","expected":"no relation"}]},{"checksum":"32237b57ca5e8a3aa09d263e761804c1e35627d3f842aac0440702c524ab94b3","generates":[{"prescription":"map each squarefree subset of primes <= z to a Fock occupation state (Pauli exclusion = squarefree kernel)","stage":"identify basis"},{"prescription":"read mu as fermion parity (-1)^F and face adjacency as one-body hopping between Fock states","stage":"identify operators"}],"honest_boundary":"Identification only -- no spectral content yet; the spectral program (13d/13e) is what tests it. The identification itself (faces = Fock basis, mu = fermion parity) is independently known (goldenphysicsproject, GitHub, contemporary 2026; priority genuinely unclear) and must be credited as such; the distinct contribution is the spectral program, not the identification.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D3","rule":"faces S of Delta_z = fermionic Fock basis over primes <= z; each prime used at most once = Pauli = squarefree kernel; mu = (-1)^F (fermion parity); face adjacency = fermionic hopping","subtitle":"Fermionic Fock identification (13a): the sieve's own materials","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"squarefree-kernel <-> Pauli exclusion","expected":"exact correspondence, native not imported"}]},{"checksum":"d20f1a2f18b4a319b9206e738c91fa7e30f73a5c13c78f45edd39b116e625f07","generates":[{"prescription":"observe the one-body terms commute and each squares to 1","stage":"commute"},{"prescription":"read the spectrum directly as {sum_p +/-(log p)/p} -- integrable by inspection, no numerics needed beyond the sanity check","stage":"diagonalize by inspection"}],"honest_boundary":"Killed as an operator candidate -- integrable by inspection; the sanity check is the entire numerical content. Do not present as anything but a kill with a clean derivation.","honest_label":"exact","id":"D4","rule":"H_2 = sum_p (log p / p)(a_p^dag + a_p); one-body hopping with the prime terms of -zeta'/zeta; [O_p,O_q]=0, O_p^2=1","subtitle":"H_2 killed by inspection (13b)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"spectrum vs dense diagonalization (z=13)","expected":"agreement to 2.4e-15"},{"check":"mean spacing ratio","expected":"<r>=0.503, spiky structured spacings"}]},{"checksum":"ab97efb8dca8aee976aece5fd03fd91995b867b6b4148947a9f2675d1cd76d1e","conventions":["use canonical p<q, r<s sectors -- summing over ALL ordered quadruples with symmetric weights gives identically zero (a_r a_s = -a_s a_r)","H_diag = sum_{p<q} (log p log q)/(pq) n_p n_q (the (zeta'/zeta)^2 semiprime terms)"],"generates":[{"prescription":"build H_2 (one-body hopping), H_diag (Fock-diagonal two-body), and the pair-hop term at z<=29 (dim<=1024) via fock_pairhop.py","stage":"assemble"},{"prescription":"set lam_0 by Frobenius-norm equality; scan 0.25x-4x","stage":"fix scale"},{"prescription":"diagonalize and compute bulk spacing statistics <r> and the spacing histogram; stress-test at z=31/37 dense and z=41 sparse Lanczos (fock_robust.py, fock_strengthen.py)","stage":"probe"}],"honest_boundary":"Shuffled-weight control ALSO gives GUE (0.524) -- this is generic two-body quantum chaos (TBRE class), not created by the arithmetic; the non-trivial content is only that the arithmetic weights are COMPATIBLE with chaos (they could have been too weak/structured). Universality class != the zeros: eigenvalues are not gamma_n; no zero detection. Finite sizes; histogram not pure Wigner yet. Delta_3 rigidity inconclusive (flat ~0.33 across L=5..40 -- likely unfolding/window artifact on the 1200-eigenvalue sample, not interpreted). Do not present 13d as a bridge plank.","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D5","rule":"H(lam) = H_2 + H_diag + lam * sum_{p,q,r,s} w_p w_q w_r w_s a_p^dag a_q^dag a_r a_s (number-conserving pair hop, w_p=(log p)/p); lam_0 fixed by ||lam_0 H_pair||_F = ||H_2+H_diag||_F","subtitle":"Pair-hopping construction H(lam) (13d): the mixing term 13c lacked","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"<r> across z>=17, all lam","expected":"0.52-0.55 (GUE 0.536, Poisson 0.386)"},{"check":"spacing histogram","expected":"level repulsion: dip at 0, peak ~0.5, tracking Wigner, far from Poisson"},{"check":"z=31 (dim 2048), lam=0.5*lam_0 and lam_0","expected":"<r>=0.528/0.531"},{"check":"z=37 (dim 4096)","expected":"<r>=0.535/0.535"},{"check":"z=41 sparse Lanczos (dim 8192), 1200 interior eigenvalues","expected":"bulk <r>=0.528"}]},{"checksum":"fc83155b1fda3def4b396cfc9b339a809bfd698cd75961ee994685b64d588b43","id":"G1","result":"no relation; Weyl's law N(Lambda) ~ C_d Vol Lambda^{d/2}: d=2 too slow by a log, d>=3 too fast, vs zeros' (T/2pi) log T","title":"L1-L3 multi-torus linkages dead by Weyl (12b)","transfer":"'multi-torus via Laplacian' is dead; 'multi-torus via dynamics' (12c/L4, Deninger's program) is the live form of the original idea","tried":"flat-T^3 Laplacian Weyl probe: 554,981 lattice points enumerated, first 300 eigenvalues vs first 300 zeta zeros (multi_torus_weyl.png)","type":"G","verdict":"killed by theorem, not difficulty"},{"checksum":"5b1271d13d3dbb1de6a3f0509d22ca998e8572046cab62ee604d1abe3317282c","id":"G2","result":"negative on three panels (heisenberg_probe.png): (i) counting is Weyl d=3, slope 3/2, vs zeros' T log T; (ii) bulk spacings rigid/degenerate (mass near 0, no level repulsion) vs the zeros' GUE-like repulsion; (iii) sequences unrelated","title":"Heisenberg nilmanifold probe negative (12d)","transfer":"genuine theta-function / Weil-representation arithmetic content in a geometric Laplacian still does not give zero statistics -- arithmetic flavor != zero spectrum; the missing operator is not 'Laplacian + theta'. Framework's computable content is now exhausted; L4 (Deninger-type dynamics) remains as formulated conjecture","tried":"exact spectrum from representation theory: (2pih)^2+2pi|h|(2k+1), mult |h|, plus the torus part; 65,401 eigenvalues enumerated (heisenberg_probe.py) -- the one non-flat computable case (theta-function spectrum via the Weil representation)","type":"G","verdict":"killed -- the honest remaining check came back negative; Node 12 CLOSED"},{"checksum":"f89c6b818a01b8e81fd816e133c3a3ed5078a39046384102cee86e0a4f50dd79","id":"G3","result":"bulk spacings track POISSON, not GUE: <r> = 0.459,0.418,0.400,0.411,0.419 (Poisson 0.386, GUE 0.536); histogram monotone decreasing, max at 0 (fock_probe.png)","title":"H_int minimal interacting Hamiltonian -- Poisson (13c)","transfer":"the interaction is Fock-diagonal -- it shifts energies but causes no transitions; all mixing comes from the integrable one-body hopping. Poisson was unsurprising in hindsight. Next construction if the fork continues: OFF-DIAGONAL two-body (pair hopping a^dag a^dag a a with arithmetic weights)","tried":"H_int = H_2 + sum_{p<q} (log p log q)/(pq) n_p n_q -- minimal interacting native Hamiltonian (one-body = zeta'/zeta prime terms, two-body = (zeta'/zeta)^2 semiprime terms); diagonalized z<=29 (dim<=1024, fock_operator.py)","type":"G","verdict":"killed; the valuable part is the understanding"},{"checksum":"4ac1d6ecf3642ae17284d5e2a345679797c0c5f52a845f9f2c3ffeeb45423c22","id":"G4","result":"no prime-frequency content: mean z-score at the 10 prime lines = -0.35 (arith), -0.36 (shuffled); GUE control 0.28 (flat noise, method unbiased). Both arith and shuffled show one broad structural hump at f~0.67 (construction-scale, not arithmetic -- identical in shuffled). Honest limits: spectral bandwidth only ~7.3 at z=29, so the lowest prime frequencies (p=2,3: <1 period across the spectrum) are weakly resolved; null is strongest at larger p; degree-10 detrending could partially absorb broad oscillations, but the GUE control through the identical pipeline shows the method creates no structure","title":"Prime-frequency probe negative -- the operator does not hear the primes (13e)","transfer":"the 'make 10a and 13d talk' attempt returns: they don't, this way -- 13d's GUE chaos carries no prime-frequency signature","tried":"asked whether the pair-hop spectrum's fluctuations oscillate at prime frequencies f_p = log(p)/2pi (the explicit-formula signature, run in reverse): z=29 spectrum, degree-10 detrended N_osc, Lomb-Scargle, vs GUE(1024) and shuffled-weight controls (fock_primefreq.py)","type":"G","verdict":"killed as a bridge attempt; 13d stands as a universality result (side chamber), not a bridge plank"},{"checksum":"baa1f00446d07376e3a98787531f73028e8511961577ba506dc30c343be86ab5","id":"G5","result":"the resonance/zero identification is imported, not derived","title":"D10 -- toroidal five-step proof (archive mining)","transfer":"prove the bridge, don't import it -- our 10a is the derived version","tried":"April-2026 toroidal five-step proof read as archaeology at the user's direction ('negative results refine the area that could possibly be positive')","type":"G","verdict":"guardrail: resonance/zero identification imported, not derived"},{"checksum":"4fb6d020bcfa8fd8353fd955408f7804d926529583a136c51246a333a8f7e1f5","id":"G6","result":"first counterexample (1129,1151)->21 at the ~190th pair; the 'era interaction' patch is post-hoc","title":"D11 -- Prime Zipper Law falsified (archive mining)","transfer":"a falsified statement stays falsified -- post-hoc patches do not reopen it","tried":"April-2026 Prime Zipper Law as stated","type":"G","verdict":"gap quantization dead"},{"checksum":"3aea6d1170447d098f9b1fd181b8f4608286226e784ecc94f16df60488f82667","id":"G7","result":"Lemma 3 keeps the test functions but the spectral side is what changed","title":"D12 -- rh_final formal compactification (archive mining)","transfer":"maps where Lax-Phillips genuinely gets stuck -- audit which side of a duality a regularization actually acts on before trusting it","tried":"April-2026 rh_final compactification read as archaeology","type":"G","verdict":"guardrail: weight engineered to delete the continuous spectrum the conclusion needs gone"},{"checksum":"48df14b2e20f177daa27aff39b3fbaee0a2426c966848ce5e2c06282dd69eeb1","id":"G8","result":"coset sums do not constitute the Chebyshev mechanism","title":"D13 -- coset-sum numerology (archive mining)","transfer":"demand the mechanism, not the numerical resemblance","tried":"April-2026 coset-sum material read as archaeology (s_watts_v2 and the 60-second piece filed without new extraction)","type":"G","verdict":"guardrail: numerology != mechanism"},{"checksum":"c138ec659a65d4500793dd5768c3cbffac91a4667a71dcc9f570fd856dd62708","from":"D2","id":"L1","rel":"supports","to":"G1","type":"L"},{"checksum":"36e6b56ee0c564805b55aa5f8d9fe939b053b5246039c1e0fbd0f7a5e1fd7da8","from":"C1","id":"L2","rel":"refines","to":"D1","type":"L"},{"checksum":"60bbe148e6724e2fa870d12b8a6bf9f2b9ea9c1deefbb82fb8bd0f17495b0b8b","from":"G3","id":"L3","rel":"causes","to":"D5","type":"L"},{"checksum":"e1ea3257aa2f03576f6f8d53d339f01d556565bfee440426faec091d6466ffe7","from":"D5","id":"L4","rel":"supports","to":"V1","type":"L"},{"checksum":"53fa0a53e32a016631d831ace2052eedb58f14a163d46d9e4eec6e302e86fa74","from":"G4","id":"L5","rel":"bounds","to":"V1","type":"L"},{"checksum":"84292b35c52510257873fbf3705b882074ba90f9035b7111fe0c25c12b946b3f","consequence":"the sieve's native Fock space with arithmetically-weighted hopping+interaction+pair-hopping is quantum-chaotic in the GUE class -- the same universality class as the zeta zeros; first operator in the hunt pointing the right way. Robustness: GUE-compatible at 4x the original dimension (z=31/37) and 8x via Lanczos (z=41); the positive is not a small-size artifact. Strengtheners queued: larger z via Lanczos (z=43, dim 16384, running), Delta_3 rigidity, density of states. Honest limits per D5 -- present as a universality result, never as zero detection.","id":"V1","status":"computationally_verified","subject":"Node 13d -- pair-hopping: FIRST POSITIVE operator signal","type":"V"}],"registry":{"C1":"C","D1":"D","D2":"D","D3":"D","D4":"D","D5":"D","G1":"G","G2":"G","G3":"G","G4":"G","G5":"G","G6":"G","G7":"G","G8":"G","L1":"L","L2":"L","L3":"L","L4":"L","L5":"L","V1":"V"},"wire_checksum":"a8e84565104e58a1aa36538957a5982f5b3e6fee11bbe7387c66f60dab386800"}:TELOMERE-CCC2-1